-- title:
--   Riemann–Roch space of a constant field conorm
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $K'$, $F$, $F'$ be fields with $K$-algebra structures making $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ compatible towers, where $K'/K$ is algebraic and separable and $F'/F$ is integral; assume moreover that the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $K'$ is all of $F'$ (hypothesis `hgen`), that every element of $F$ algebraic over $K$ lies in the image of $K$ (hypothesis `hconst`), and that $F'/K'$ has principal divisors in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.HasPrincipalDivisors`](def/AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup.html#L217): for every nonzero $f \in F'$ there is a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on the places of $F'/K'$ whose value at each place $W$ is $\operatorname{ord}_W(f)$ and whose degree is $0$. Here a place of $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring, and a divisor is a finitely supported $\mathbb{Z}$-valued function on places. For a divisor $D$ of $F/K$, its constant field pullback [`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.pullbackConstants K' F' D`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ConstantFieldPullback.html#L176) is obtained additively from the values of $D$: the divisor attached to a single place $v$ with multiplicity $n$ is $\sum_{w} n \cdot e_w \, [w]$, the sum over the places $w$ in [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.fiberConstants K' F' v`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ConstantFieldPullback.html#L150) of $F'/K'$ attached to $v$, where $e_w$ is the ramification index over $F$ of the associated place [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.forgetConstants w`](def/AlgebraicCurve_ConstantFieldPullback.html#L17) of $F'/K$. Writing $\mathcal{L}(D) = \{f : v(f) \le \exp(D\,v) \text{ for all places } v\}$ for the Riemann–Roch space, a $K$-submodule of $F$, the assertion is that $\mathcal{L}(\text{pullbackConstants } D)$ equals the $K'$-span in $F'$ of the image of $\mathcal{L}(D)$ under $F \to F'$.
--
--   This is the spanning half of the classical theorem on algebraic separable constant field extensions (Stichtenoth, Theorem 3.6.3(d)): a $K$-basis of $\mathcal{L}(D)$ spans $\mathcal{L}(\operatorname{Con} D)$ over $K'$. It is used to show that a divisor of $F/K$ whose constant field pullback is principal is itself principal, hence that the induced map of divisor class groups is injective.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_lSpace_pullbackConstants_eq_span_of_isConstantFieldExtension.lean

